{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412766","formula":"C₁₀H₁₅NO₃","hill":"C10H15NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":15.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Metanephrine","ru":"Метанефрин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Metanephrine, also known as metadrenaline, is a metabolite of epinephrine (also known as adrenaline) created by action of catechol-O-methyl transferase on epinephrine. An article in the Journal of the American Medical Association, 2002, indicated that the measurement of plasma free levels of the metanephrines group of molecules (including metanephrine and normetanephrine) is the best tool in the diagnosis of pheochromocytoma, an adrenal medullary neoplasm.","ru":"Метанефрин — метаболит адреналина, образуемый с помощью фермента COMT."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":21100,"mass":197.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"CNCC(C1=CC(=C(C=C1)O)OC)O","inchikey":"JWJCTZKFYGDABJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-[1-hydroxy-2-(methylamino)ethyl]-2-methoxyphenol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"21100","atoms":29,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.086,"y":-0.76,"z":1.715,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.42,"y":1.61,"z":0.684,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.786,"y":-0.53,"z":-0.447,"el":"O"},{"x":3.991,"y":0.228,"z":-0.207,"el":"N"},{"x":1.799,"y":-0.817,"z":0.312,"el":"C"},{"x":0.323,"y":-0.738,"z":0.113,"el":"C"},{"x":2.547,"y":0.322,"z":-0.409,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.372,"y":0.41,"z":0.494,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.363,"y":-1.812,"z":-0.455,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.752,"y":0.483,"z":0.308,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.743,"y":-1.739,"z":-0.64,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.438,"y":-0.591,"z":-0.259,"el":"C"},{"x":4.682,"y":1.295,"z":-0.914,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.554,"y":2.64,"z":-0.294,"el":"C"},{"x":2.178,"y":-1.782,"z":-0.048,"el":"H"},{"x":2.217,"y":1.292,"z":-0.019,"el":"H"},{"x":2.309,"y":0.291,"z":-1.48,"el":"H"},{"x":0.146,"y":1.249,"z"